,{"style":{"color":"rgba(255,255,255,0.2)","fontSize":12},"children":"›"}],["$","span",null,{"style":{"fontFamily":"'JetBrains Mono', monospace","fontSize":11,"color":"#C8A34D","fontWeight":600,"letterSpacing":"0.05em"},"children":"Pricing"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"display":"flex","alignItems":"center","gap":12,"marginBottom":20,"flexWrap":"wrap"},"children":[["$","span",null,{"style":{"background":"rgba(200,163,77,0.15)","color":"#C8A34D","padding":"4px 10px","borderRadius":4,"fontSize":11,"fontWeight":600,"fontFamily":"'JetBrains Mono', monospace","letterSpacing":"0.05em"},"children":"Pricing"}],["$","span",null,{"style":{"fontSize":12,"color":"rgba(255,255,255,0.4)","fontFamily":"'JetBrains Mono', monospace"},"children":"May 2, 2025"}],["$","span",null,{"style":{"fontSize":12,"color":"rgba(255,255,255,0.4)","fontFamily":"'JetBrains Mono', monospace"},"children":["· ","7 min read"]}]]}],["$","h1",null,{"style":{"fontFamily":"'Syne', sans-serif","fontSize":"clamp(28px, 4vw, 42px)","fontWeight":700,"color":"#fff","lineHeight":1.15,"marginBottom":0,"letterSpacing":"-0.02em"},"children":"Commercial Cleaning Costs: What to Expect Per Square Foot in 2026"}]]}]]}],"$undefined",["$","article",null,{"style":{"maxWidth":720,"margin":"0 auto","padding":"48px 24px 64px"},"children":[[["$","p","0",{"style":{"fontSize":18,"color":"#1A2B1F","lineHeight":1.8,"marginBottom":32,"fontWeight":500},"children":"One of the most common questions facility managers ask is: what should commercial cleaning actually cost? The answer depends on several factors — but there are industry benchmarks that help you evaluate whether a proposal is reasonable. This guide breaks down pricing by facility type, frequency, and region so you can negotiate from a position of knowledge."}],["$","h2","1",{"style":{"fontFamily":"'Syne', sans-serif","fontSize":22,"fontWeight":700,"color":"#1A2B1F","lineHeight":1.25,"marginTop":40,"marginBottom":16,"letterSpacing":"-0.01em"},"children":"Average Cost Ranges by Facility Type"}],["$","p","2",{"style":{"fontSize":16,"color":"#4A5E52","lineHeight":1.8,"marginBottom":20},"children":"Commercial cleaning is typically priced per square foot per cleaning, or as a monthly rate based on square footage and frequency. For standard office buildings, expect $0.05-$0.15 per sq ft per cleaning for basic janitorial service. Medical offices run higher at $0.12-$0.25 due to compliance requirements. Schools typically fall in the $0.08-$0.18 range depending on facility age and scope. Government buildings average $0.07-$0.15. Daycare centers, due to specialized product requirements, typically run $0.10-$0.22. These ranges reflect the Northeast and Mid-Atlantic markets — Southern and rural markets may be 15-25% lower."}],["$","h2","3",{"style":{"fontFamily":"'Syne', sans-serif","fontSize":22,"fontWeight":700,"color":"#1A2B1F","lineHeight":1.25,"marginTop":40,"marginBottom":16,"letterSpacing":"-0.01em"},"children":"What Drives Price Differences"}],["$","p","4",{"style":{"fontSize":16,"color":"#4A5E52","lineHeight":1.8,"marginBottom":20},"children":"Several factors push pricing up or down. Frequency matters — five-day-per-week service costs more than three-day, but the per-cleaning rate typically decreases. Facility complexity plays a role: medical offices with terminal cleaning requirements cost more than open-plan offices. Building age and condition affect pricing — older buildings with worn flooring require more labor. After-hours or overnight service typically costs 10-15% more than daytime cleaning. And specialized services like floor care, disinfection, and window cleaning are usually priced separately from base janitorial."}],["$","h2","5",{"style":{"fontFamily":"'Syne', sans-serif","fontSize":22,"fontWeight":700,"color":"#1A2B1F","lineHeight":1.25,"marginTop":40,"marginBottom":16,"letterSpacing":"-0.01em"},"children":"Red Flags in Cleaning Proposals"}],["$","p","6",{"style":{"fontSize":16,"color":"#4A5E52","lineHeight":1.8,"marginBottom":20},"children":"Be cautious of bids significantly below market range — they typically indicate corners being cut on staffing, products, insurance, or wages. Other red flags include no site visit before quoting, vague scope descriptions without specific task lists, no mention of insurance or certifications, lack of quality verification methods, and reluctance to provide references from similar facilities. The lowest price almost always leads to the fastest turnover of cleaning companies."}],["$","h2","7",{"style":{"fontFamily":"'Syne', sans-serif","fontSize":22,"fontWeight":700,"color":"#1A2B1F","lineHeight":1.25,"marginTop":40,"marginBottom":16,"letterSpacing":"-0.01em"},"children":"Getting the Best Value"}],["$","p","8",{"style":{"fontSize":16,"color":"#4A5E52","lineHeight":1.8,"marginBottom":20},"children":"Value isn't the lowest price — it's the best outcome per dollar spent. To maximize value, create a detailed scope of work before requesting quotes, compare at least three proposals against the same scope, ask about bundling services for volume discounts, negotiate multi-year contracts for rate stability, and prioritize companies with quality verification systems that prevent the need for rework and rebidding."}],["$","div","9",{"style":{"background":"#F0F7F2","borderLeft":"3px solid #1B7A3D","padding":"20px 24px","borderRadius":"0 8px 8px 0","margin":"32px 0"},"children":["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":15,"color":"#1A2B1F","lineHeight":1.7,"fontWeight":500,"margin":0},"children":"GreenPoint provides transparent, scope-based pricing with no hidden fees. Every proposal starts with a complimentary facility walkthrough so our quote matches your actual needs — not a generic estimate. Request a walkthrough today."}]}]],["$","div",null,{"style":{"borderTop":"1px solid #E2EBE5","marginTop":48,"paddingTop":32,"display":"flex","flexDirection":"column","gap":16},"children":[["$","div",null,{"style":{"display":"flex","alignItems":"center","gap":14},"children":[["$","